arXiv:2603.10219v1 [stat.ML] 10 Mar 2026</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line" lang="en">
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="p1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\uselogo</span>
</div>
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Tor Lattimore
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_correspondent"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Corresponding author: </span>lattimore@google.com
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><span id="id1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\thepa</span>
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">We study a continuous-time diffusion approximation of policy gradient for <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-armed stochastic bandits.
We prove that with a learning rate <math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=O(\Delta^{2}/\log(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=O(\Delta^{2}/\log(n))</annotation></semantics></math> the regret is <math id="abstract1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(k\log(k)\log(n)/\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(k\log(k)\log(n)/\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="abstract1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the horizon
and <math id="abstract1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> the minimum gap.
Moreover, we construct an instance with only logarithmically many arms for which the regret is linear unless <math id="abstract1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=O(\Delta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=O(\Delta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Policy gradient is a classical and widely used reinforcement learning algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sutton et al., 1998</a>)</cite>.
Our focus is on the dynamics of policy gradient with the softmax policy class on Gaussian bandits.
Even in this simple setup, only the two-armed setting is really properly understood.
We opt for the unusual simplification of studying a continuous-time diffusion approximation
of the policy gradient algorithm.
We believe (but do not prove) that this is a high-quality approximation. This approach comes with a number of advantages.
Most straightforwardly, the randomness arising from the sampling of actions is removed, which slightly simplifies the analysis.
More significantly, by switching to continuous time we can exploit the vast literature on stochastic differential equations.
Needless to say, we hope the proof ideas can be generalised to discrete time eventually, but for now we are happy to settle with simpler analysis
and new means for understanding a delicate problem.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Basic notation</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We let <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟏</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{0}</annotation></semantics></math> denote vectors of all ones and zeros, respectively, and with the dimension always obvious from the context.
The standard basis vectors in <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1},\ldots,e_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1},\ldots,e_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and
the identity matrix is <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Id</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Id}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a vector <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{diag}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{diag}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the diagonal matrix with <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> as its diagonal.
We let <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\cdot\right\|_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\cdot\right\|_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-norm and for positive definite <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|x\right\|_{A}=(x^{\top}Ax)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|x\right\|_{A}=(x^{\top}Ax)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We let <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be suitably small/large absolute constants.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bandit notation</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There are <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> actions and the horizon is <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume purely for the sake of simplifying cluttered expressions that <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\max(3,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\max(3,k)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We will consider Gaussian rewards with mean <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and standard deviation <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We assume that
<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\geq\mu_{\star}=\mu_{1}&gt;\mu_{2}\geq\cdots\geq\mu_{k}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\geq\mu_{\star}=\mu_{1}&gt;\mu_{2}\geq\cdots\geq\mu_{k}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\sigma\right\|_{\infty}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\sigma\right\|_{\infty}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
We let <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{a}=\mu_{1}-\mu_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{a}=\mu_{1}-\mu_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a vector <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> we let <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> be the softmax policy with <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\theta)_{a}\propto\exp(\theta_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\theta)_{a}\propto\exp(\theta_{a})</annotation></semantics></math>.
In discrete time the learner sequentially selects actions <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and observes rewards <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}=\mu_{A_{t}}+\sigma_{A_{t}}\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}=\mu_{A_{t}}+\sigma_{A_{t}}\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is an independent sequence of standard Gaussian random variables.
The regret in the discrete time setting is</p>
<table id="S1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{Reg}_{n}=n\mu_{\star}-\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mu_{A_{t}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{Reg}_{n}=n\mu_{\star}-\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mu_{A_{t}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\star}=\max_{a\in\{1,\ldots,k\}}\mu_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\star}=\max_{a\in\{1,\ldots,k\}}\mu_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Our main focus, however, is on a continuous time approximation of the discrete process.
Let <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be a standard <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional Brownian motion on some probability space and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be its natural filtration.
In the continuous-time bandit problem the learner selects a policy <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a process in the simplex adapted to the natural filtration associated with the process <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the
stochastic differential equation (SDE) given by</p>
<table id="S1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})\mu\operatorname{d}\!t+\operatorname{diag}(\sqrt{\pi_{t}})\Sigma^{1/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})\mu\operatorname{d}\!t+\operatorname{diag}(\sqrt{\pi_{t}})\Sigma^{1/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\operatorname{diag}(\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\operatorname{diag}(\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The existence of a solution to <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> might be hard to resolve for complex policies <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> but will be straightforward for our choice of a softmax policy
updated using (continuous time) policy gradient.
The regret in continuous time is
<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Reg}_{n}=\int_{0}^{n}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Reg}_{n}=\int_{0}^{n}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}=\mu_{\star}-\langle\pi_{t},\mu\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}=\mu_{\star}-\langle\pi_{t},\mu\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note, <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is always used for the <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional Brownian motion driving the process <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">some</span> standard <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional Brownian motion,
but not always the same one.
The classical policy gradient algorithm is given in <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Bandit notation ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, while its continuous time approximation is in <a href="#algorithm2" title="In Bandit notation ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="algorithm1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="25" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 482.22 25" width="482.22"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,25) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(241.11,0) translate(0,12.5)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6E6;" fill="#E6E6E6"><path d="M -240.83 -12.22 h 481.66 v 24.45 h -481.66 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -236.22 -3.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:34.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="472.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="algorithm1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:34.14em;">
<span id="algorithm1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="algorithm1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_left ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">args</span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">learning</span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">rate</span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}=\bm{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}=\bm{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">for</span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">to</span><span id="lstnumberx3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}=\pi(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}=\pi(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx5" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">sample</span><span id="lstnumberx5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">from</span><span id="lstnumberx5.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx5.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx5.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">observe</span><span id="lstnumberx5.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{A_{t}},\sigma_{A_{t}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{A_{t}},\sigma_{A_{t}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx6" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">update</span><span id="lstnumberx6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall a\,\,\theta_{t+1,a}=\theta_{t,a}+\eta(\bm{1}_{A_{t}=a}-\pi_{t,a})Y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall a\,\,\theta_{t+1,a}=\theta_{t,a}+\eta(\bm{1}_{A_{t}=a}-\pi_{t,a})Y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Algorithm 1: </span> 
Discrete time policy gradient.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="algorithm2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="25.52" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 482.22 25.52" width="482.22"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,25.52) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(241.11,0) translate(0,12.76)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6E6;" fill="#E6E6E6"><path d="M -240.83 -12.48 h 481.66 v 24.97 h -481.66 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -236.22 -4.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:34.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.29)" width="472.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="algorithm2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:34.14em;">
<span id="algorithm2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="algorithm2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_left ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx7" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">args</span><span id="lstnumberx7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">learning</span><span id="lstnumberx7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">rate</span><span id="lstnumberx7.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx8" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}=\bm{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}=\bm{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx9" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">for</span><span id="lstnumberx9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,n]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx10" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}=\pi(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}=\pi(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx11" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">observe</span><span id="lstnumberx11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})\mu\operatorname{d}\!t+\operatorname{diag}(\sqrt{\pi_{t}})\Sigma^{1/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})\mu\operatorname{d}\!t+\operatorname{diag}(\sqrt{\pi_{t}})\Sigma^{1/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx12" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">update</span><span id="lstnumberx12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}=\eta(\operatorname{Id}-\pi_{t}\bm{1}^{\top})\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}=\eta(\operatorname{Id}-\pi_{t}\bm{1}^{\top})\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Algorithm 2: </span> 
Continuous time policy gradient.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Contribution</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We study the regret of <a href="#algorithm2" title="In Bandit notation ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
On the positive side, we show that if <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq c\Delta_{2}^{2}/\log(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq c\Delta_{2}^{2}/\log(n)</annotation></semantics></math>,
then the regret is at most</p>
<table id="S1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{Ck\log(k)\log(n)}{\eta}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{Ck\log(k)\log(n)}{\eta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">More negatively, we show that if <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\Omega(\Delta_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\Omega(\Delta_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exist instances with logarithmically many actions and a very large horizon where the regret is <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(n\Delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(n\Delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Related work</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mei et al. (2020)</a></cite> study policy gradient in discrete time without noise and show <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/t)</annotation></semantics></math> convergence.
A similar result in continuous time is provided by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Walton (2020)</a></cite>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mei et al. (2023)</a></cite> also prove almost sure convergence, but with the assumption that the learning rate is <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\Delta_{2}^{2}/k^{3/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\Delta_{2}^{2}/k^{3/2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mei et al. (2024)</a></cite> show that policy gradient converges to a unique optimal action almost surely with any learning rate
and that asymptotically the regret is <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log(t))</annotation></semantics></math> with non-specified problem-dependent constants.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Baudry et al. (2025)</a></cite>
show that setting the learning rate <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is needed for logarithmic regret and that this can fail when <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math> they argue that <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> must be <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/k)</annotation></semantics></math> and prove that the regret is <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(k^{2}\log(n)/\Delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(k^{2}\log(n)/\Delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\sim\Delta_{2}/k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\sim\Delta_{2}/k</annotation></semantics></math> and
all suboptimal arms have the same gap.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Policy gradient in continuous time</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In discrete time the classical policy gradient algorithm specified to <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-armed bandits
is derived as follows.
The value function is <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(\theta)=\langle\pi(\theta),\mu\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(\theta)=\langle\pi(\theta),\mu\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and its gradient is</p>
<table id="S2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v^{\prime}(\theta)=(\operatorname{diag}(\pi)-\pi\pi^{\top})\mu\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v^{\prime}(\theta)=(\operatorname{diag}(\pi)-\pi\pi^{\top})\mu\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This quantity is not observed, but is classically estimated in round <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> using Monte-Carlo by</p>
<table id="S2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\nabla}_{t}=(\operatorname{Id}-\pi_{t}\bm{1}^{\top})e_{A_{t}}Y_{t}=(\operatorname{Id}-\pi_{t}\bm{1}^{\top})e_{A_{t}}Y_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mo>∇</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\nabla}_{t}=(\operatorname{Id}-\pi_{t}\bm{1}^{\top})e_{A_{t}}Y_{t}=(\operatorname{Id}-\pi_{t}\bm{1}^{\top})e_{A_{t}}Y_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The policy gradient update with learning rate <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is then</p>
<table id="S2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{t+1}=\theta_{t}+\eta\widehat{\nabla}_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mo>∇</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{t+1}=\theta_{t}+\eta\widehat{\nabla}_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">In continuous time there are two ways to proceed.
One option is to approximate the discrete time stochastic process <math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> by a continuous process with matching variance
and drift. Alternatively, the mechanism for deriving the policy gradient method can be repeated from first principles in continuous
time. <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> remains the same in continuous time. Because the drift of the continuous-time process <math id="S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, an unbiased continuous-time estimator of <math id="S2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\prime}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\prime}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\operatorname{Id}-\pi_{t}\bm{1}^{\top})\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\operatorname{Id}-\pi_{t}\bm{1}^{\top})\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the continuous-time policy gradient algorithm is naturally defined by the stochastic process</p>
<table id="S2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta(\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})-\pi_{t}\pi_{t}^{\top})\mu\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\operatorname{diag}(\sqrt{\pi_{t}})\Sigma^{1/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}-\eta\pi_{t}\langle\sqrt{\pi_{t}},\Sigma^{1/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}\rangle\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta(\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})-\pi_{t}\pi_{t}^{\top})\mu\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\operatorname{diag}(\sqrt{\pi_{t}})\Sigma^{1/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}-\eta\pi_{t}\langle\sqrt{\pi_{t}},\Sigma^{1/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">This is equivalent to approximating the discrete time policy gradient algorithm by matching the mean and variance.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Elementary properties</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before the serious analysis, we start with a collection of elementary results about the vectors <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> defined in
<a href="#algorithm2" title="In Bandit notation ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
The proofs either appear inline or in the appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">conservation</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a=1}^{k}\theta_{t,a}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a=1}^{k}\theta_{t,a}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> almost surely.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute the definition of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to show that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\bm{1},\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\bm{1},\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The next lemma shows that with high probability <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> never becomes too negative.
This is intuitive since by <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 1 (conservation). ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{b}\theta_{t,b}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{b}\theta_{t,b}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,a}\leq\exp(\theta_{t,a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,a}\leq\exp(\theta_{t,a})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, if <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes very negative, then
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes vanishingly small and the updates by policy gradient to <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> become negligible.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for all actions <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\{1,\ldots,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\{1,\ldots,k\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\inf_{t\leq n}\theta_{t,a}\leq-\log\left(n/\delta\right)\right)\leq\delta\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\inf_{t\leq n}\theta_{t,a}\leq-\log\left(n/\delta\right)\right)\leq\delta\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The standard behaviour of an effective bandit algorithm is that suboptimal arms are slowly eliminated as they are identified as being statistically
suboptimal. For randomised algorithms this roughly means that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\pi_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\pi_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a measure of the number of actions that still appear competitive.
The following lemma relates this quantity to the magnitude of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math> showing that as <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math> grows, the number of arms that appear competitive
reduces:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,a}\in[-\log(n/\delta),k\log(n/\delta)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,a}\in[-\log(n/\delta),k\log(n/\delta)]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,1}\geq\max_{a}\theta_{t,a}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,1}\geq\max_{a}\theta_{t,a}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\pi_{t,1}}\leq\frac{6k\log(n/\delta)}{\theta_{t,1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\pi_{t,1}}\leq\frac{6k\log(n/\delta)}{\theta_{t,1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The conditions in <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> are interesting. The first holds with high probability by <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 1 (conservation). ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Later we will prove the second holds with high probability
when the learning rate is sufficiently small and is equivalent to <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,1}/\pi_{t,a}\geq 1/e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,1}/\pi_{t,a}\geq 1/e</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Upper bounds</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To avoid clutter we assume that the variance matrix is the identity: <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\operatorname{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\operatorname{Id}</annotation></semantics></math>. This corresponds to the assumption in the discrete time
setting that the reward distributions for all actions have unit variance. All results in this section still hold when <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\preceq\operatorname{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\preceq\operatorname{Id}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As a warmup, we start with the two-armed setting, which is straightforward and also well-understood in the discrete time setting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Baudry et al., 2025</a>, Theorem 1)</cite>.
In fact, our proof follows theirs almost without modification.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\Delta_{2}/\eta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\Delta_{2}/\eta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then with <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]\leq\frac{a}{2\Delta_{2}}\log\left(1+\frac{2(a+1)n\Delta_{2}^{2}}{a^{2}}\right)+\frac{a^{2}}{2(a-1)\Delta_{2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]\leq\frac{a}{2\Delta_{2}}\log\left(1+\frac{2(a+1)n\Delta_{2}^{2}}{a^{2}}\right)+\frac{a^{2}}{2(a-1)\Delta_{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Abbreviate <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}=\pi_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}=\pi_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Starting with the same regret decomposition as proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Baudry et al. (2025)</a></cite>, the regret is</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{Reg}_{n}=\Delta_{2}\int_{0}^{n}(1-\pi_{t})\operatorname{d}\!t=\Delta_{2}\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})\operatorname{d}\!t+\Delta_{2}\int_{0}^{n}(1-\pi_{t})^{2}\operatorname{d}\!t\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{Reg}_{n}=\Delta_{2}\int_{0}^{n}(1-\pi_{t})\operatorname{d}\!t=\Delta_{2}\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})\operatorname{d}\!t+\Delta_{2}\int_{0}^{n}(1-\pi_{t})^{2}\operatorname{d}\!t\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}=\exp(bZ_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}=\exp(bZ_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. By Itô’s rule,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[M_{n}]-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[M_{n}]-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})M_{t}(2b\eta\Delta_{2}+2b^{2}\eta^{2})\operatorname{d}\!t\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})M_{t}\Delta_{2}^{2}(2b/a+2b^{2}/a^{2})\operatorname{d}\!t\right]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})M_{t}(2b\eta\Delta_{2}+2b^{2}\eta^{2})\operatorname{d}\!t\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})M_{t}\Delta_{2}^{2}(2b/a+2b^{2}/a^{2})\operatorname{d}\!t\right]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}=\pi_{t}/(1-\pi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}=\pi_{t}/(1-\pi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and in this case</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[M_{n}]=1+\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}^{2}\Delta_{2}^{2}(2/a+2/a^{2})\right]\leq 1+\left(2/a+2/a^{2}\right)n\Delta_{2}^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[M_{n}]=1+\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}^{2}\Delta_{2}^{2}(2/a+2/a^{2})\right]\leq 1+\left(2/a+2/a^{2}\right)n\Delta_{2}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, since <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> has drift <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\eta\Delta_{2}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\eta\Delta_{2}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})\operatorname{d}\!t\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}\pi_{t}(1-\pi_{t})\operatorname{d}\!t\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}[Z_{n}]}{2\eta}\leq\frac{\log(\mathbb{E}[M_{n}])}{2\eta}\leq\frac{a}{2\Delta_{2}}\log\left(1+\frac{2(a+1)n\Delta_{2}^{2}}{a^{2}}\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}[Z_{n}]}{2\eta}\leq\frac{\log(\mathbb{E}[M_{n}])}{2\eta}\leq\frac{a}{2\Delta_{2}}\log\left(1+\frac{2(a+1)n\Delta_{2}^{2}}{a^{2}}\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the inequalities follow from Jensen, <a href="#S3.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and because <math id="S3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\Delta_{2}/\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\Delta_{2}/\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the other term in the decomposition, let <math id="S3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=-1</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}=(1-\pi_{t})/\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}=(1-\pi_{t})/\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[M_{n}]-1=\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}(1-\pi_{t})^{2}\Delta_{2}^{2}(2/a^{2}-2/a)\right]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[M_{n}]-1=\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}(1-\pi_{t})^{2}\Delta_{2}^{2}(2/a^{2}-2/a)\right]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-negative and <math id="S3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}(1-\pi_{t})^{2}\operatorname{d}\!t\right]\leq\frac{a^{2}}{2(a-1)\Delta_{2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{n}(1-\pi_{t})^{2}\operatorname{d}\!t\right]\leq\frac{a^{2}}{2(a-1)\Delta_{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Combining <a href="#S3.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> with <a href="#S3.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> yields the bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and by choosing <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> very slowly one obtains the regret for the (non-anytime) algorithm
of <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]\sim\frac{\log(n)}{2\Delta_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]\sim\frac{\log(n)}{2\Delta_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which appears to contradict the lower bound by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lai and Robbins (1985)</a></cite>.
The reason there is no contradiction is that the learning rate depends on <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and in this scenario the
classical lower bound does not apply and the <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\log(n)}{2\Delta_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\log(n)}{2\Delta_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> regret is optimal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Garivier et al., 2016</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The argument above does not generalise to the situation where there are more than two actions.
Not only is the problem more difficult to analyse, the learning rate needs to be considerably smaller and the regret is correspondingly much worse.
We will prove the following:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8\log(2n^{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8\log(2n^{2})}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]=O\left(\frac{k\log(k)\log(n)}{\eta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]=O\left(\frac{k\log(k)\log(n)}{\eta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We start with a straightforward lemma governing the dynamics of <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(\frac{\pi_{t,1}}{\pi_{t,a}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(\frac{\pi_{t,1}}{\pi_{t,a}})</annotation></semantics></math> that reveals the main challenge when <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t,a}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t,a}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\left[\pi_{t,a}\Delta_{a}+(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})R_{t}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,a}-(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})^{2}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\left[\pi_{t,a}\Delta_{a}+(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})R_{t}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,a}-(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})^{2}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard Brownian motion.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The expression in <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 7. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> is revealing. If we are to prove the algorithm is learning, then we must show that <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> increases with time for <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Naturally this will be easiest to prove if the SDE associated with <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t,a}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t,a}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> has positive drift and well-controlled noise.
Regrettably, however, this is not the case. The drift <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\pi_{t,a}\Delta_{a}+\eta(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\pi_{t,a}\Delta_{a}+\eta(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be negative if <math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,1}&lt;\pi_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,1}&lt;\pi_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math>
and the regret is large. If there were no noise, then an elementary analysis of the differential equation would show that the drift is always positive
because at initialisation <math id="S3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,1}\geq\pi_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,1}\geq\pi_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> and the positive drift ensures this stays true throughout the trajectory.
The following lemma shows that when <math id="S3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is suitably small, then <math id="S3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> can be lower-bounded with high probability.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8\log(2n/\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8\log(2n/\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\inf_{t\leq n}Z_{t,a}\leq-\Delta_{2}/2)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\inf_{t\leq n}Z_{t,a}\leq-\Delta_{2}/2)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Abbreviate <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}=Z_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}=Z_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau=\inf\{t:Z_{t}=-\Delta_{2}/2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\inf\{t:Z_{t}=-\Delta_{2}/2\}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(t)=\eta^{2}\int_{0}^{t}(\pi_{u,1}+\pi_{u,a}-(\pi_{u,1}-\pi_{u,a})^{2})\operatorname{d}\!u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(t)=\eta^{2}\int_{0}^{t}(\pi_{u,1}+\pi_{u,a}-(\pi_{u,1}-\pi_{u,a})^{2})\operatorname{d}\!u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(\cdot)=s^{-1}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(\cdot)=s^{-1}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> be its inverse.
Lastly, let <math id="S3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{s(t)}=Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{s(t)}=Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition, <math id="S3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{t\leq n}Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{t\leq n}Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> has the same law as <math id="S3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{s\leq s(n)}U_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{s\leq s(n)}U_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, when <math id="S3.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U_{s}\geq-\Delta_{2}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{s}\geq-\Delta_{2}/2</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!U_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!U_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\eta}\left[\frac{\pi_{t(s),a}\Delta_{a}+\pi_{t(s),a}(\exp(U_{s})-1)R_{t(s)}}{\pi_{t(s),1}+\pi_{t(s),a}-(\pi_{t(s),1}-\pi_{t(s),a})^{2}}\right]\operatorname{d}\!s+\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\eta}\left[\frac{\pi_{t(s),a}\Delta_{a}+\pi_{t(s),a}(\exp(U_{s})-1)R_{t(s)}}{\pi_{t(s),1}+\pi_{t(s),a}-(\pi_{t(s),1}-\pi_{t(s),a})^{2}}\right]\operatorname{d}\!s+\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{2\eta}\left[\frac{\pi_{t(s),a}\Delta_{a}}{\pi_{t(s),1}+\pi_{t(s),a}}\right]\operatorname{d}\!s+\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}=\frac{\Delta_{a}}{2\eta(\exp(U_{s})+1)}\operatorname{d}\!s+\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{2\eta}\left[\frac{\pi_{t(s),a}\Delta_{a}}{\pi_{t(s),1}+\pi_{t(s),a}}\right]\operatorname{d}\!s+\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}=\frac{\Delta_{a}}{2\eta(\exp(U_{s})+1)}\operatorname{d}\!s+\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the inequality holds because <math id="S3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t(s)}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t(s)}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\exp(U_{s})-1\geq\exp(-\Delta_{2}/2)-1\geq-\Delta_{2}/2\geq-\Delta_{a}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≥</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(U_{s})-1\geq\exp(-\Delta_{2}/2)-1\geq-\Delta_{2}/2\geq-\Delta_{a}/2</annotation></semantics></math>, which means the numerator is positive.
Looking at this relation, when the learning rate is small relative to <math id="S3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the process has considerable positive drift when <math id="S3.p6.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U_{s}\in[-\Delta_{2}/2,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{s}\in[-\Delta_{2}/2,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Formally, since <math id="S3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(n)\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(n)\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> and by a comparison to the SDE in <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Proposition 16. ‣ Appendix A Technical inequalities ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>,
<math id="S3.p6.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\inf\{U_{s}:0\leq s\leq s(n)\}\leq-\Delta_{2}/2\right)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\inf\{U_{s}:0\leq s\leq s(n)\}\leq-\Delta_{2}/2\right)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We are now in a position to prove <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=1/n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t,a}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t,a}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> and define a stopping time <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\tau=\inf\left\{t\leq n:\min_{a\in 2,\ldots,k}Z_{t,a}\leq-\Delta_{2}/2\text{ or }\min_{a\in 1,\ldots,k}\theta_{t,a}\leq-\log(n/\delta)\right\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext> or </mtext><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau=\inf\left\{t\leq n:\min_{a\in 2,\ldots,k}Z_{t,a}\leq-\Delta_{2}/2\text{ or }\min_{a\in 1,\ldots,k}\theta_{t,a}\leq-\log(n/\delta)\right\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and a union bound, with probability at least <math id="S3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2k\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2k\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=n</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 1 (conservation). ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows that <math id="S3.p8.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\log(n/\delta)\leq\theta_{t,1}=-\sum_{a=2}^{k}\theta_{t,a}\leq k\log(n/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log(n/\delta)\leq\theta_{t,1}=-\sum_{a=2}^{k}\theta_{t,a}\leq k\log(n/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u&gt;-\log(n/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u&gt;-\log(n/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}(u)=\frac{6k\log(n/\delta)}{u+1+\log(n/\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}(u)=\frac{6k\log(n/\delta)}{u+1+\log(n/\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the function that appeared in <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
Then let</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi(u)=\int_{0}^{u}\psi^{\prime}(v)\operatorname{d}\!v=6k\log(n/\delta)\log\left(\frac{u+1+\log(n/\delta)}{1+\log(n/\delta)}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi(u)=\int_{0}^{u}\psi^{\prime}(v)\operatorname{d}\!v=6k\log(n/\delta)\log\left(\frac{u+1+\log(n/\delta)}{1+\log(n/\delta)}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Later we will use the fact that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi(k\log(n/\delta))\leq 6k\log(n/\delta)\log(1+k)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi(k\log(n/\delta))\leq 6k\log(n/\delta)\log(1+k)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, for <math id="S3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u&gt;-\log(n/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u&gt;-\log(n/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi^{\prime\prime}(u)=-\frac{6k\log(n/\delta)}{(u+1+\log(n/\delta))^{2}}\geq-\psi^{\prime}(u)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi^{\prime\prime}(u)=-\frac{6k\log(n/\delta)}{(u+1+\log(n/\delta))^{2}}\geq-\psi^{\prime}(u)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}=\eta^{2}\pi_{t,1}(1-\pi_{t,1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}=\eta^{2}\pi_{t,1}(1-\pi_{t,1})</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition <math id="S3.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t,1}=\eta\pi_{t,1}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t,1}=\eta\pi_{t,1}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
and hence by Itô’s formula,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!\psi(\theta_{t,1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!\psi(\theta_{t,1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t,1}+\frac{1}{2}\psi^{\prime\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}^{2}\operatorname{d}\!t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t,1}+\frac{1}{2}\psi^{\prime\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}^{2}\operatorname{d}\!t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\geq}}\left[\eta\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}R_{t}-\frac{\eta^{2}\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}(1-\pi_{t,1})}{2}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(a)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\geq}}\left[\eta\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}R_{t}-\frac{\eta^{2}\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}(1-\pi_{t,1})}{2}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\geq}}\left[\eta\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}R_{t}-\frac{\eta^{2}\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}R_{t}}{2\Delta_{2}}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(b)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\geq}}\left[\eta\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}R_{t}-\frac{\eta^{2}\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}R_{t}}{2\Delta_{2}}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{2}\eta\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(c)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{2}\eta\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\pi_{t,1}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{2}\eta R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(d)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{2}\eta R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\psi^{\prime}(\theta_{t,1})\sigma_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <span id="S3.p8.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(a)</span> follows from <a href="#S3.E7" title="In Proof of . ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>,
<span id="S3.p8.6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(b)</span> since <math id="S3.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}\geq(1-\pi_{t,1})\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}\geq(1-\pi_{t,1})\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<span id="S3.p8.6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(c)</span> since <math id="S3.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="S3.p8.6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(d)</span> follows from <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
Taking expectations and rearranging in combination with <a href="#S3.E6" title="In Proof of . ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{\tau}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{\tau}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\eta}\mathbb{E}[\psi(\theta_{\tau,1})]\leq\frac{12k\log(n/\delta)\log(1+k)}{\eta}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\eta}\mathbb{E}[\psi(\theta_{\tau,1})]\leq\frac{12k\log(n/\delta)\log(1+k)}{\eta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;n)\leq 2k\delta=2k/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;n)\leq 2k\delta=2k/n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]\leq 2k+\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{\tau}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]\leq 2k+\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{\tau}]</annotation></semantics></math> and the argument is complete.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 9</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The analysis in <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> can be improved by refining the bound <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}\leq\Delta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}\leq\Delta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
With this change one obtains the same bound as <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> but the condition on <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> can be relaxed to
<math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\tilde{O}(\Delta_{2}^{2}/\Delta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\tilde{O}(\Delta_{2}^{2}/\Delta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequentially, when all actions have the same suboptimality gap and <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\frac{c\Delta_{2}}{\log(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\frac{c\Delta_{2}}{\log(n)}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]=O\left(\frac{k\log(k)\log(n)^{2}}{\Delta_{2}}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]=O\left(\frac{k\log(k)\log(n)^{2}}{\Delta_{2}}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Lower bound</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows that when there are only two actions, then setting <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> just slightly smaller than <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> leads to near-optimality of policy gradient.
The next construction shows that when there are more than two actions the correct choice of <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> can be as small as <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and in general
no choice leads to near-optimal regret in the sense of being
remotely close to the lower bound by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lai and Robbins (1985)</a></cite>.
The fundamental difference is that when <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>, the drift of <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math> is always positive. When there are more arms, this only holds on trajectories
that are well-behaved in the sense that <math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> never gets too negative for <math id="S4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Lower bound construction</h3>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The poor behaviour of policy gradient is most dramatic when <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is such that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=(0,\Delta_{2},1,\ldots,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=(0,\Delta_{2},1,\ldots,1)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> close to zero.
The following arguments can be made to work with <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\operatorname{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\operatorname{Id}</annotation></semantics></math> but are simplified considerably by instead letting <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\operatorname{diag}(e_{1}+e_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\operatorname{diag}(e_{1}+e_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> so that the only noise arises from the first two actions.
What happens in this scenario is that for a long time actions <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> are nearly statistically indistinguishable.
Since actions <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math> are very suboptimal, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math> decreases rapidly and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math> increase.
But they do not increase together at the same rate. Rather, unless the learning rate is very small, the dynamics of policy gradient effectively ‘picks a winner’ in <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> at random
and by the time <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> is negligible for <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>, it turns out that either <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math> is nearly <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
From then on policy gradient behaves as if the bandit has two actions, but with a potentially very disadvantageous initialisation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 10</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=(0,\Delta_{2},1,\ldots,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=(0,\Delta_{2},1,\ldots,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\operatorname{diag}(1,1,0,\ldots,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\operatorname{diag}(1,1,0,\ldots,0)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq C\log(n/\Delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq C\log(n/\Delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and
learning rate bounded in <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\Delta_{2}^{2}\leq\eta\leq c/k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\Delta_{2}^{2}\leq\eta\leq c/k</annotation></semantics></math>,
the regret of continuous policy gradient (<a href="#algorithm2" title="In Bandit notation ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]=\Omega(n\Delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]=\Omega(n\Delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 11</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The assumption that <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq c/k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq c/k</annotation></semantics></math> is for simplicity in the analysis and can be removed at the price of a slightly more complicated proof.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In full gory detail the proof is embarrassingly intricate.
We try to present the high-level argument in the main body and defer the fiddly computations to the appendix.
Alternatively, you can skip all the analysis and look at <a href="#A6.F1" title="In Appendix F Experiments ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> in <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Experiments ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>, which illustrates the striking behaviour of the discrete time policy gradient on
the instance in <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 10. ‣ Lower bound construction ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. You may also wonder if the lower bound might hold with <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>. We believe the answer is no, which is partially supported by
the results in <a href="#A6.F2" title="In Appendix F Experiments ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 10. ‣ Lower bound construction ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Abbreviate <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=k-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=k-2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,3+}=\sum_{a=3}^{k}\pi_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,3+}=\sum_{a=3}^{k}\pi_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the probability assigned to all but the first two actions.
Our argument revolves around showing that with constant probability <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math> grows much faster than <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math> for the initial period when
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,3+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,3+}</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing rapidly.
Let <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=\theta_{t,1}+\theta_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=\theta_{t,1}+\theta_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}=\theta_{t,1}-\theta_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}=\eta\pi_{t,3+}(1-\pi_{t,3+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}=\eta\pi_{t,3+}(1-\pi_{t,3+})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(t)=\int_{0}^{t}C_{u}\operatorname{d}\!u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(t)=\int_{0}^{t}C_{u}\operatorname{d}\!u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mapsto t(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mapsto t(s)</annotation></semantics></math> be its inverse.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 12</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=2/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=2/m</annotation></semantics></math> and
define a stopping time <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> as the first time that any of the following holds:</p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S4.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(a)</span></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=n</annotation></semantics></math>; or</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S4.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(b)</span></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\tau}\notin((1-\Delta_{2})s(\tau)-1,s(\tau)+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\tau}\notin((1-\Delta_{2})s(\tau)-1,s(\tau)+1)</annotation></semantics></math>; or</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S4.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(c)</span></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\tau}\geq 2\operatorname{arcsinh}\left(\sqrt{\eta}(e^{-s(\tau)}/4-1/16)e^{(1-\epsilon)s(\tau)/2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arcsinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\tau}\geq 2\operatorname{arcsinh}\left(\sqrt{\eta}(e^{-s(\tau)}/4-1/16)e^{(1-\epsilon)s(\tau)/2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>; or</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S4.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(d)</span></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\tau)=s_{\max}\triangleq\frac{1}{1-\epsilon}[\log(400/\eta)+\log(n)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\tau)=s_{\max}\triangleq\frac{1}{1-\epsilon}[\log(400/\eta)+\log(n)]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By our assumption that the variance only arises from the first two actions it follows that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,a}=\theta_{t,b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,a}=\theta_{t,b}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>,
which by <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 1 (conservation). ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and the definition <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=\theta_{t,1}+\theta_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=\theta_{t,1}+\theta_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math> means that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta_{t,a}=-S_{t}/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,a}=-S_{t}/m</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\pi_{t,1}}{\pi_{t,3+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\pi_{t,1}}{\pi_{t,3+}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m}\exp\left(\frac{S_{t}+Z_{t}}{2}+\frac{S_{t}}{m}\right)\triangleq G_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m}\exp\left(\frac{S_{t}+Z_{t}}{2}+\frac{S_{t}}{m}\right)\triangleq G_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that if <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, then by the inequality <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{arcsinh}(x)\leq-\log(-2x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>arcsinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{arcsinh}(x)\leq-\log(-2x)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{t}\leq\min\left(1,\log\left(\frac{400}{\eta}\right)-(1-\epsilon)s(t)\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>400</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{t}\leq\min\left(1,\log\left(\frac{400}{\eta}\right)-(1-\epsilon)s(t)\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Dynamics and intuition</h3>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By substituting the definitions and crude bounding we obtain the following:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\big[1-\frac{\pi_{t,2}}{1-\pi_{t,3+}}\Delta_{2}\big]C_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\sqrt{\eta\pi_{t,3+}C_{t}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\quad\text{and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mtext>and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big[1-\frac{\pi_{t,2}}{1-\pi_{t,3+}}\Delta_{2}\big]C_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\sqrt{\eta\pi_{t,3+}C_{t}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\quad\text{and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\big[\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})+\tanh(Z_{t}/2)\big]C_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\sqrt{\eta\sigma_{t}^{2}C_{t}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\big[\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})+\tanh(Z_{t}/2)\big]C_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\sqrt{\eta\sigma_{t}^{2}C_{t}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1-\tanh(Z_{t}/2)^{2}\leq\sigma_{t}^{2}\leq 1+4G_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1-\tanh(Z_{t}/2)^{2}\leq\sigma_{t}^{2}\leq 1+4G_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The tedious calculation establishing the above is deferred to the last step.
You will surely notice that these SDEs have been massaged so that the drift terms depend linearly on <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the diffusion terms depend linearly on <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{C_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{C_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which suggests we might make progress by changing time using the clock <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(t)=\int_{0}^{t}C_{u}\operatorname{d}\!u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(t)=\int_{0}^{t}C_{u}\operatorname{d}\!u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Rather than moving immediately to the formalities, let us spend a moment to argue informally.
The SDE in <a href="#S4.E9" title="In Step 1: Dynamics and intuition ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> is very well-behaved after a time change.
Since <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is small and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,2}\leq\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}=1-\pi_{t,3+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,2}\leq\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}=1-\pi_{t,3+}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!S_{t(s)}\approx\operatorname{d}\!s+\sqrt{\eta\pi_{t(s),3+}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!S_{t(s)}\approx\operatorname{d}\!s+\sqrt{\eta\pi_{t(s),3+}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which implies that with high probability <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t(s)}\approx s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t(s)}\approx s</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The SDE in <a href="#S4.E10" title="In Step 1: Dynamics and intuition ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> is much more complicated. At initialisation <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t}=1/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t}=1/m</annotation></semantics></math> is relatively small, so that</p>
<table id="S4.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t(s)}\approx[\Delta_{2}+\tanh(Z_{t(s)}/2)]\operatorname{d}\!s+\sqrt{\eta}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t(s)}\approx[\Delta_{2}+\tanh(Z_{t(s)}/2)]\operatorname{d}\!s+\sqrt{\eta}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|z|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|z|</annotation></semantics></math> is small, then <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(z/2)\approx z/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(z/2)\approx z/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, when <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{t(s)}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{t(s)}|</annotation></semantics></math> is small, a reasonable approximation for a solution (see <a href="#Thmtheorem17" title="Remark 17 (method of integrating factors). ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Remark</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) is</p>
<table id="S4.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{t(s)}\approx 2(\exp(s/2)-1)\Delta_{2}+\sqrt{\eta}\exp(s/2)\int_{0}^{s}\exp(-u/2)\operatorname{d}\!W_{u}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{t(s)}\approx 2(\exp(s/2)-1)\Delta_{2}+\sqrt{\eta}\exp(s/2)\int_{0}^{s}\exp(-u/2)\operatorname{d}\!W_{u}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which means that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t(s)}</annotation></semantics></math> has approximate law <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(2(\exp(s/2)-1)\Delta_{2},\eta(\exp(s)-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(2(\exp(s/2)-1)\Delta_{2},\eta(\exp(s)-1))</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, provided that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is suitably larger than <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the noise dominates and with roughly constant probability <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{t(s)}|\approx\exp(s/2)\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{t(s)}|\approx\exp(s/2)\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{sign}(Z_{t(s)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{sign}(Z_{t(s)})</annotation></semantics></math> is close to uniform on <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{-1,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{-1,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, if <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\approx\log(1/\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\approx\log(1/\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{t(s)}|\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{t(s)}|\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math>. At this point <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(Z_{t(s)}/2)\approx\operatorname{sign}(Z_{t(s)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(Z_{t(s)}/2)\approx\operatorname{sign}(Z_{t(s)})</annotation></semantics></math>
and the drift term is roughly constant and depending on the sign the process drifts up or down at a roughly linear rate.
Hence a reasonable ansatz is that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{t(s)}|\approx s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{t(s)}|\approx s</annotation></semantics></math> for large <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> with the sign roughly uniform when <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently larger than <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This turns out to be the correct rate.
As a consequence, we can expect that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\approx s(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\approx s(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}\approx-s(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}\approx-s(t)</annotation></semantics></math> with roughly constant probability.
Hence <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,1}=(S_{t}+Z_{t})/2\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,1}=(S_{t}+Z_{t})/2\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,2}=(S_{t}-Z_{t})/2\approx s(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,2}=(S_{t}-Z_{t})/2\approx s(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, which at minimum implies that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math> does not grow much larger than <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math>
and implies linear regret.
The challenge is we need a sample path result and the additional terms in <a href="#S4.E10" title="In Step 1: Dynamics and intuition ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> need to be handled carefully.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Handling the additional terms is unsurprisingly non-trivial. Indeed, they are what causes the argument above to fail asymptotically, which it must because for any learning rate
policy gradient does learn asymptotically.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Formal details</h3>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following proposition formalises the ansatz in the previous step.
The proof is based on a technical comparison to the standard linear SDE and is deferred to <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 14</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> either <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=n</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\tau)=s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\tau)=s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Hence it suffices to show that on this event <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{n}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t\geq cn\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{n}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t\geq cn\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
There are two cases. When <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=n</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,1}\leq e\pi_{t,2}\leq e(1-\pi_{t,1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,1}\leq e\pi_{t,2}\leq e(1-\pi_{t,1})</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,1}\leq e/(1+e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,1}\leq e/(1+e)</annotation></semantics></math>, from which it follows
that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Reg}_{n}=\Omega(n\Delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Reg}_{n}=\Omega(n\Delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose instead that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\tau)=s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\tau)=s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, by <a href="#S4.E8" title="In Proof of . ‣ Lower bound construction ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{\tau}\leq\log\left(\frac{400}{\eta}\right)-(1-\epsilon)s_{\max}=-\log(n)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>400</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{\tau}\leq\log\left(\frac{400}{\eta}\right)-(1-\epsilon)s_{\max}=-\log(n)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{\tau}\geq(1-\Delta_{2})s_{\max}-1\geq(1-\epsilon)s_{\max}-1=\log\left(\frac{400n}{\eta}\right)-1\geq\log(n/\eta)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{\tau}\geq(1-\Delta_{2})s_{\max}-1\geq(1-\epsilon)s_{\max}-1=\log\left(\frac{400n}{\eta}\right)-1\geq\log(n/\eta)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\tau,1}\leq\exp(Z_{\tau})\leq\frac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\tau,1}\leq\exp(Z_{\tau})\leq\frac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and since <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq c/k\leq c/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq c/k\leq c/m</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\tau,3+}\leq m\exp\left(-\frac{S_{\tau}}{m}-\frac{S_{\tau}-Z_{\tau}}{2}\right)\leq\frac{m\eta}{n}\leq 1/n\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\tau,3+}\leq m\exp\left(-\frac{S_{\tau}}{m}-\frac{S_{\tau}-Z_{\tau}}{2}\right)\leq\frac{m\eta}{n}\leq 1/n\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,2}\geq 1-2/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,2}\geq 1-2/n</annotation></semantics></math> and from this a straightforward argument shows that with high probability the algorithm never recovers:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\sup_{t\geq\tau}\pi_{t,1}\geq 1/2\,\bigg|\,\mathcal{F}_{\tau}\right)\leq 1/2\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\sup_{t\geq\tau}\pi_{t,1}\geq 1/2\,\bigg|\,\mathcal{F}_{\tau}\right)\leq 1/2\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that with constant probability <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,1}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,1}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]=\Omega(n\Delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Reg}_{n}]=\Omega(n\Delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> as required.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4: The calculations</h3>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We promised the concrete calculations. By definition</p>
<table id="S4.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\pi_{t,1}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\left[\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,1}-\pi_{t,1}^{3/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,1}-\pi_{t,1}\sqrt{\pi_{t,2}}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,2}\right]\text{ and }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\pi_{t,1}R_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\left[\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,1}-\pi_{t,1}^{3/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,1}-\pi_{t,1}\sqrt{\pi_{t,2}}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,2}\right]\text{ and }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t,2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\pi_{t,2}\left[R_{t}-\Delta_{2}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\left[\sqrt{\pi_{t,2}}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,2}-\pi_{t,2}^{3/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,2}-\pi_{t,2}\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,1}\right]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\pi_{t,2}\left[R_{t}-\Delta_{2}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\left[\sqrt{\pi_{t,2}}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,2}-\pi_{t,2}^{3/2}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,2}-\pi_{t,2}\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}}\operatorname{d}\!B_{t,1}\right]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The calculation for <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> follows by substituting the definitions.
For <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S4.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\left[\pi_{t,2}\Delta_{2}+(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2})R_{t}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}-(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2})^{2}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\left[\pi_{t,2}\Delta_{2}+(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2})R_{t}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}-(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2})^{2}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\alpha_{t}\Delta_{2}+\tanh(Z_{t}/2)\right]C_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\sqrt{\eta\sigma_{t}^{2}C_{t}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\alpha_{t}\Delta_{2}+\tanh(Z_{t}/2)\right]C_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\sqrt{\eta\sigma_{t}^{2}C_{t}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> defined by</p>
<table id="S4.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\pi_{t,2}(1+\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2})}{\pi_{t,3+}(1-\pi_{t,3+})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\pi_{t,2}(1+\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2})}{\pi_{t,3+}(1-\pi_{t,3+})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1+\frac{4\pi_{t,1}\pi_{t,2}}{\pi_{t,3+}(1-\pi_{t,3+})}-(1-\pi_{t,3+})\left(\frac{\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2}}{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}}\right)^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1+\frac{4\pi_{t,1}\pi_{t,2}}{\pi_{t,3+}(1-\pi_{t,3+})}-(1-\pi_{t,3+})\left(\frac{\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2}}{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}}\right)^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,2}\leq\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}=1-\pi_{t,3+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,2}\leq\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}=1-\pi_{t,3+}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{t}=\frac{\pi_{t,2}(2\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,3+})}{\pi_{t,3+}(1-\pi_{t,3+})}\leq 1+2G_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{t}=\frac{\pi_{t,2}(2\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,3+})}{\pi_{t,3+}(1-\pi_{t,3+})}\leq 1+2G_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Moreover, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2}}{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}}=\tanh(Z_{t}/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,2}}{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,2}}=\tanh(Z_{t}/2)</annotation></semantics></math> so that
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\tanh(Z_{t}/2)^{2}\leq\sigma_{t}^{2}\leq 1+4G_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\tanh(Z_{t}/2)^{2}\leq\sigma_{t}^{2}\leq 1+4G_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Discussion</h2>

<section id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Continuous time vs discrete time</h3>

<div id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When the learning rate is small, the continuous time and discrete time processes are extremely similar.
Even for larger learning rates, the noise terms contract asymptotically in both cases, suggesting that the diffusion approximation may be good
for any learning rate once the algorithm reaches the asymptotic regime.
We believe our proof technique for the upper bound is likely to translate to the discrete time setting, probably with only a little tedium.
Proving the lower bound in discrete time is probably more challenging and arguably less worthwhile.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Refining the lower bound</h3>

<div id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our upper bound is <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{O}(k/\Delta_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{O}(k/\Delta_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The lower bound shows that this is not in general improvable when <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is logarithmic.
An interesting direction is to extend the lower bound construction to introduce a linear dependence on <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-dependence</h3>

<div id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Baudry et al. (2025)</a></cite> constructed a lower bound showing that the learning rate needs to be <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/k)</annotation></semantics></math> and speculated that the correct learning rate might be around <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}/k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}/k</annotation></semantics></math>.
Our upper bound holds without assuming that <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is less than <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/k)</annotation></semantics></math>, suggesting that this is a transient requirement where the continuous time and discrete time setups are
not comparable. Moreover, our lower bound shows that in certain cases the learning rate needs to be <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\Delta_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\Delta_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> in order to achieve sublinear regret.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Logarithmic factors</h3>

<div id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The upper bound in <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> relies on the assumption that <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq c\Delta_{2}^{2}/\log(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq c\Delta_{2}^{2}/\log(n)</annotation></semantics></math>. One may wonder if this logarithmic term in the denominator can be dropped.
The argument in <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> is quite crude, so there may be room for improvement there.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
