<span class="ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited">Cited by: <a href="#S1.p1.1" title="1 Introduction ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§1</span></a>.
</span></li>
<li id="bib.bib5" class="ltx_bibitem ltx_bib_article"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_bib_author-year ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Walton (2020)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_author">N. Walton</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_title">A short note on soft-max and policy gradients in bandits problems</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_journal">arXiv preprint arXiv:2007.10297</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited">Cited by: <a href="#S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" title="Related work ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§1</span></a>.
</span></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Technical inequalities</h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 15</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=a\operatorname{d}\!t+\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=a\operatorname{d}\!t+\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\inf_{t\geq 0}X_{t}\leq-\epsilon\right)\leq\exp(-2a\epsilon)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\inf_{t\geq 0}X_{t}\leq-\epsilon\right)\leq\exp(-2a\epsilon)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Use the fact that <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}=\exp(-2aX_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}=\exp(-2aX_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale and Doob’s maximal inequality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 16</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=\frac{a}{\exp(X_{t})+1}\operatorname{d}\!t+\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=\frac{a}{\exp(X_{t})+1}\operatorname{d}\!t+\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\inf\{X_{t}:0\leq t\leq n\}\leq-\epsilon\right)\leq(1+\sqrt{n}/2)\exp\left(-\frac{2a\epsilon}{e+1}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\inf\{X_{t}:0\leq t\leq n\}\leq-\epsilon\right)\leq(1+\sqrt{n}/2)\exp\left(-\frac{2a\epsilon}{e+1}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\geq\frac{e+1}{2\epsilon}\log((1+\sqrt{n}/2)/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\geq\frac{e+1}{2\epsilon}\log((1+\sqrt{n}/2)/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\inf\{X_{t}:0\leq t\leq n\}\leq-\epsilon)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\inf\{X_{t}:0\leq t\leq n\}\leq-\epsilon)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Obviously the drift is positive everywhere and
when <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{t}\in(-\infty,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}\in(-\infty,1]</annotation></semantics></math> the drift term is at least <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a/(e+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a/(e+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, letting <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\inf\{t:X_{t}\in\{-\epsilon,1\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\inf\{t:X_{t}\in\{-\epsilon,1\}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that
<math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}(X_{\tau}=-\epsilon)\leq\exp(-2a\epsilon/(e+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(X_{\tau}=-\epsilon)\leq\exp(-2a\epsilon/(e+1))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, since <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> has positive drift everywhere, the number of down-crossings <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of the interval <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded in expectation by
the number of down-crossings of a Brownian motion in the same time interval, which by Doob’s down-crossing lemma is at most
<math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[D_{n}]\leq\mathbb{E}[\max(0,B_{n})]\leq\sqrt{n}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[D_{n}]\leq\mathbb{E}[\max(0,B_{n})]\leq\sqrt{n}/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore
<math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\inf\{X_{t}:0\leq t\leq n\}\leq-\epsilon\right)\leq(1+\sqrt{n}/2)\exp(-(2a\epsilon)(e+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\inf\{X_{t}:0\leq t\leq n\}\leq-\epsilon\right)\leq(1+\sqrt{n}/2)\exp(-(2a\epsilon)(e+1))</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}=\exp(-\theta_{t,a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}=\exp(-\theta_{t,a})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 1 (conservation). ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> there exists a <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,b}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,b}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}\leq\exp(\theta_{t,b}-\theta_{t,a})=\pi_{t,b}/\pi_{t,a}\leq 1/\pi_{t,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}\leq\exp(\theta_{t,b}-\theta_{t,a})=\pi_{t,b}/\pi_{t,a}\leq 1/\pi_{t,a}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, by Itô’s formula</p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=M_{t}\left[\eta\pi_{t,a}(\bar{\mu}_{t}-\mu_{a})+\frac{\eta^{2}\pi_{t,a}(1-\pi_{t,a})}{2}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta M_{t}\sqrt{\pi_{t,a}(1-\pi_{t,a})}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=M_{t}\left[\eta\pi_{t,a}(\bar{\mu}_{t}-\mu_{a})+\frac{\eta^{2}\pi_{t,a}(1-\pi_{t,a})}{2}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta M_{t}\sqrt{\pi_{t,a}(1-\pi_{t,a})}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left[\eta+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta M_{t}\sqrt{\pi_{t,a}(1-\pi_{t,a})}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left[\eta+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\eta M_{t}\sqrt{\pi_{t,a}(1-\pi_{t,a})}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, since <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, by Markov’s inequality</p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\sup_{t\leq n}M_{t}\geq\frac{1}{\delta}+\frac{n}{\delta}\left[\eta+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\right]\right)\leq\delta\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\sup_{t\leq n}M_{t}\geq\frac{1}{\delta}+\frac{n}{\delta}\left[\eta+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\right]\right)\leq\delta\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which after naively simplifying <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq c</annotation></semantics></math> implies that with probability at least <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,a}\geq-\log\left(n/\delta\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,a}\geq-\log\left(n/\delta\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Elementary properties ‣ 2 Policy gradient in continuous time ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leq 0\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leq 0\leq b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\{x\in[a,b]^{m}:\sum_{i=1}^{m}x_{i}=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\{x\in[a,b]^{m}:\sum_{i=1}^{m}x_{i}=0\}</annotation></semantics></math>
and let <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of measurable functions from <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,m]\to[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,m]\to[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{m}f(x)\operatorname{d}\!x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{m}f(x)\operatorname{d}\!x=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{x\in K}\left\|\exp(x)\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{x\in K}\left\|\exp(x)\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\max_{f\in F}\int_{0}^{m}\exp(f(x))\operatorname{d}\!x=m\left[\frac{b}{b-a}\exp(a)-\frac{a}{b-a}\exp(b)\right]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>m</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\max_{f\in F}\int_{0}^{m}\exp(f(x))\operatorname{d}\!x=m\left[\frac{b}{b-a}\exp(a)-\frac{a}{b-a}\exp(b)\right]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To reduce clutter we drop the time indices.
Hence, by the previous display with <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\theta_{1}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\theta_{1}+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=-\log(n/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=-\log(n/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp(\theta)\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp(\theta)\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq k\left[\frac{\theta_{1}+1}{\theta_{1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\left(\frac{\delta}{n}\right)+\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{\theta_{1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\exp(\theta_{1}+1)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq k\left[\frac{\theta_{1}+1}{\theta_{1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\left(\frac{\delta}{n}\right)+\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{\theta_{1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\exp(\theta_{1}+1)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{k\delta}{n}+\frac{k\log(n/\delta)}{\theta_{1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\exp(\theta_{1}+1)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{k\delta}{n}+\frac{k\log(n/\delta)}{\theta_{1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\exp(\theta_{1}+1)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}\geq\theta_{a}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}\geq\theta_{a}-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a=1}^{k}\theta_{a}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a=1}^{k}\theta_{a}=0</annotation></semantics></math> it follows that <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}\geq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}\geq-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore</p>
<table id="A3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\pi_{1}}=\left\|\exp(\theta)\right\|_{1}\exp(-\theta_{1})\leq e\left[\frac{k\delta}{n}+\frac{k\log(n/\delta)}{\theta_{1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\right]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\pi_{1}}=\left\|\exp(\theta)\right\|_{1}\exp(-\theta_{1})\leq e\left[\frac{k\delta}{n}+\frac{k\log(n/\delta)}{\theta_{1}+1+\log(n/\delta)}\right]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The result now follows by crudely simplifying the constants.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 7. ‣ 3 Upper bounds ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t,a}=b_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\langle\sigma_{t},\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t,a}=b_{t}\operatorname{d}\!t+\langle\sigma_{t},\operatorname{d}\!B_{t}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t,a}=\langle e_{1}-e_{a},\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!Z_{t,a}=\langle e_{1}-e_{a},\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>
Substituting the definition of <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the drift is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle e_{1}-e_{a},(\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})-\pi_{t}\pi_{t}^{\top})\mu\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle e_{1}-e_{a},(\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})-\pi_{t}\pi_{t}^{\top})\mu\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{t,1}(\mu_{1}-\bar{\mu}_{t})-\pi_{t,a}(\mu_{a}-\bar{\mu}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{t,1}(\mu_{1}-\bar{\mu}_{t})-\pi_{t,a}(\mu_{a}-\bar{\mu}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{t,1}R_{t}-\pi_{t,a}(R_{t}-\Delta_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{t,1}R_{t}-\pi_{t,a}(R_{t}-\Delta_{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{t,a}\Delta_{a}+(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})R_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{t,a}\Delta_{a}+(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})R_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly, the diffusion coefficient is
<math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\left\|e_{1}-e_{a}\right\|_{\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})-\pi_{t}\pi_{t}^{\top}}=\eta\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,a}-(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\left\|e_{1}-e_{a}\right\|_{\operatorname{diag}(\pi_{t})-\pi_{t}\pi_{t}^{\top}}=\eta\sqrt{\pi_{t,1}+\pi_{t,a}-(\pi_{t,1}-\pi_{t,a})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem14" title="Proposition 14. ‣ Step 2: Formal details ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a></h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The analysis of <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is straightforward.
We have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!S_{t(s)}\leq\operatorname{d}\!s+\sqrt{\eta\pi_{t(s),3+}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!S_{t(s)}\leq\operatorname{d}\!s+\sqrt{\eta\pi_{t(s),3+}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t(s)}\leq s+\sqrt{\eta}W_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t(s)}\leq s+\sqrt{\eta}W_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and by the maximal inequality, with probability at least <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(t)\leq s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(t)\leq s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{t(s)}\leq s+\sqrt{2\eta s_{\max}\log(1/\delta)}&lt;s+1\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{t(s)}\leq s+\sqrt{2\eta s_{\max}\log(1/\delta)}&lt;s+1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Similarly, <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!S_{t(s)}\geq(1-\Delta_{2})\operatorname{d}\!s+\sqrt{\eta\pi_{t(s),3+}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!S_{t(s)}\geq(1-\Delta_{2})\operatorname{d}\!s+\sqrt{\eta\pi_{t(s),3+}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and with probability at least <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(t)\leq s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(t)\leq s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{t(s)}&gt;(1-\Delta_{2})s-1\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{t(s)}&gt;(1-\Delta_{2})s-1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The last two parts involve <math id="A5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and are more challenging.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 17</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">method of integrating factors</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem17.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Remember that the linear SDE with <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=\left[A_{t}+B_{t}X_{t}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+C_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{d}\!X_{t}=\left[A_{t}+B_{t}X_{t}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+C_{t}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> has the solution</p>
<table id="A5.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t}=e^{\beta(t)}\left[\int_{0}^{t}e^{-\beta(u)}A_{u}\operatorname{d}\!u+\int_{0}^{t}e^{-\beta(u)}C_{u}\operatorname{d}\!W_{u}\right]\text{ with }\beta(t)=\int_{0}^{t}B_{u}\operatorname{d}\!u\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t}=e^{\beta(t)}\left[\int_{0}^{t}e^{-\beta(u)}A_{u}\operatorname{d}\!u+\int_{0}^{t}e^{-\beta(u)}C_{u}\operatorname{d}\!W_{u}\right]\text{ with }\beta(t)=\int_{0}^{t}B_{u}\operatorname{d}\!u\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the identities <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sinh^{\prime}(x)=\cosh(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>sinh</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cosh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sinh^{\prime}(x)=\cosh(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cosh^{\prime}(x)=\sinh(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>cosh</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cosh^{\prime}(x)=\sinh(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cosh(x)=\sqrt{1+\sinh^{2}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cosh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sinh</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cosh(x)=\sqrt{1+\sinh^{2}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=\sinh(Z_{t}/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=\sinh(Z_{t}/2)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Itô’s formula,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!U_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!U_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})\sqrt{1+U_{t}^{2}}+U_{t}+\frac{\eta(1+4G_{t})U_{t}}{4}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\eta\sigma_{t}^{2}(1+U_{t}^{2})C_{t}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})\sqrt{1+U_{t}^{2}}+U_{t}+\frac{\eta(1+4G_{t})U_{t}}{4}\right]\operatorname{d}\!t+\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\eta\sigma_{t}^{2}(1+U_{t}^{2})C_{t}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Let us start by upper bounding the drift term. Suppose that <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}\leq\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}\leq\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textrm{Drift}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Drift</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textrm{Drift}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})\sqrt{1+U_{t}^{2}}+U_{t}+\frac{\eta(1+4G_{t})U_{t}}{4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})\sqrt{1+U_{t}^{2}}+U_{t}+\frac{\eta(1+4G_{t})U_{t}}{4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})(1+\sqrt{2})+U_{t}\left(1-\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})\bm{1}_{U_{t}&lt;0}\right)+\frac{\eta(1+4G_{t})}{4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(a)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})(1+\sqrt{2})+U_{t}\left(1-\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})\bm{1}_{U_{t}&lt;0}\right)+\frac{\eta(1+4G_{t})}{4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[6(\Delta_{2}+\eta)(1+G_{t})+U_{t}\left(1-\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})\bm{1}_{U_{t}&lt;0}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(b)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[6(\Delta_{2}+\eta)(1+G_{t})+U_{t}\left(1-\Delta_{2}(1+2G_{t})\bm{1}_{U_{t}&lt;0}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[6(\Delta_{2}+\eta)(1+G_{t})+U_{t}\left(1-\Delta_{2}\left(1+\frac{400}{m\sqrt{\eta}}\right)\bm{1}_{U_{t}&lt;0}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(c)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>400</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{C_{t}}{2}\left[6(\Delta_{2}+\eta)(1+G_{t})+U_{t}\left(1-\Delta_{2}\left(1+\frac{400}{m\sqrt{\eta}}\right)\bm{1}_{U_{t}&lt;0}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\leq}}C_{t}\left[3\left(\Delta_{2}+\eta+\epsilon\sqrt{\eta}\right)(1+G_{t})+\frac{U_{t}\left(1-\epsilon\right)}{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(d)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\leq}}C_{t}\left[3\left(\Delta_{2}+\eta+\epsilon\sqrt{\eta}\right)(1+G_{t})+\frac{U_{t}\left(1-\epsilon\right)}{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(e)}}}}}{{\leq}}C_{t}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}(1+G_{t})+\frac{U_{t}\left(1-\epsilon\right)}{2}\right]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(e)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>96</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(e)}}}}}{{\leq}}C_{t}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}(1+G_{t})+\frac{U_{t}\left(1-\epsilon\right)}{2}\right]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <span id="A5.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(a)</span> follows from the inequality <math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{1+u^{2}}\leq 1+\sqrt{2}-u\bm{1}_{u&lt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{1+u^{2}}\leq 1+\sqrt{2}-u\bm{1}_{u&lt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A5.p2.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(b)</span> by direct simplification.
<span id="A5.p2.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(c)</span> by the bound on <math id="A5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> below (<a href="#A5.E13" title="In Exact solution ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).
<span id="A5.p2.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(d)</span> since <math id="A5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\eta}\geq C\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\eta}\geq C\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}\leq 1/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}\leq 1/m</annotation></semantics></math> and by the definition of <math id="A5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=2/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=2/m</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A5.p2.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(e)</span> follows from the assumptions on <math id="A5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, by a comparison, there exists a coupling between <math id="A5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{s(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{s(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> and another process <math id="A5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}\leq V_{s(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}\leq V_{s(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A5.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!V_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{d}\!V_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[3(\Delta_{2}+\eta)(1+G_{t(s)})+\frac{\epsilon\sqrt{\eta}}{2}+\frac{V_{s}\left(1-\epsilon\right)}{2}\right]+\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\eta\gamma_{s}^{2}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[3(\Delta_{2}+\eta)(1+G_{t(s)})+\frac{\epsilon\sqrt{\eta}}{2}+\frac{V_{s}\left(1-\epsilon\right)}{2}\right]+\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\eta\gamma_{s}^{2}}\operatorname{d}\!W_{s}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\gamma_{s}^{2}\leq(1+4G_{t(s)})(1+V_{s}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\gamma_{s}^{2}\leq(1+4G_{t(s)})(1+V_{s}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Exact solution</h3>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall now that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{t}=\frac{1}{m}\exp\left(\frac{S_{t}+Z_{t}}{2}+\frac{S_{t}}{m}\right)\leq\frac{8}{m}\exp\left(s(t)/2\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{t}=\frac{1}{m}\exp\left(\frac{S_{t}+Z_{t}}{2}+\frac{S_{t}}{m}\right)\leq\frac{8}{m}\exp\left(s(t)/2\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we used <a href="#Thmtheorem12" title="Definition 12. ‣ Proof of . ‣ Lower bound construction ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> to argue that for <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\leq s(t)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\leq s(t)+1</annotation></semantics></math> and the assumption that <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{\max}+1)/m\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{\max}+1)/m\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Alternatively, <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be bounded in another way for <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A5.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{t}=\frac{1}{m}\exp\left(\frac{S_{t}+Z_{t}}{2}+\frac{S_{t}}{m}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{t}=\frac{1}{m}\exp\left(\frac{S_{t}+Z_{t}}{2}+\frac{S_{t}}{m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{200}{m\sqrt{\eta}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>200</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{200}{m\sqrt{\eta}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which again follows from <a href="#Thmtheorem12" title="Definition 12. ‣ Proof of . ‣ Lower bound construction ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> and <a href="#S4.E8" title="In Proof of . ‣ Lower bound construction ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and the assumption that <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{\max}+1)/m\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{\max}+1)/m\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the method of integrating factors (<a href="#Thmtheorem17" title="Remark 17 (method of integrating factors). ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Remark</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A5.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle V_{s}=e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u/2}(1+G_{t(u)})\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>96</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{s}=e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u/2}(1+G_{t(u)})\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the quadratic variation of the martingale</p>
<table id="A5.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle M_{s}=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u/2}\gamma_{u}\operatorname{d}\!W_{u}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{s}=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u/2}\gamma_{u}\operatorname{d}\!W_{u}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\inf\{s:V_{s}=1\text{ or }[M]_{s}=3/4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\inf\{s:V_{s}=1\text{ or }[M]_{s}=3/4\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Constant probability event</h3>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By definition, <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]_{s}\leq 3/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]_{s}\leq 3/2</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider the event <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{u}+u\in[-1/8,1/8]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{u}+u\in[-1/8,1/8]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\leq 3/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\leq 3/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
An elementary argument shows that <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(E)&gt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(E)&gt;c</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the remainder we show the following hold on <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(a)</span></span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]_{s}&lt;3/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]_{s}&lt;3/4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(b)</span></span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{s}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{s}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(c)</span></span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{s}\leq-\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{40}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>40</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{s}\leq-\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{40}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">These imply that <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and in particular by our comparison to <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{s(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{s(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> the claim holds.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounding the quadratic variation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that by definition, if <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{s}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{s}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and by <a href="#A5.E14" title="In Exact solution ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{s}^{2}\leq\max\left(1,4\eta e^{(1-\epsilon)s}\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{s}^{2}\leq\max\left(1,4\eta e^{(1-\epsilon)s}\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we used the fact that when <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]_{s}\leq 3/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]_{s}\leq 3/2</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{[M]_{s}}\geq-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{[M]_{s}}\geq-2</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition the quadratic variation is</p>
<table id="A5.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[M]_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[M]_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u}\gamma_{u}^{2}\operatorname{d}\!u\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u}\gamma_{u}^{2}\operatorname{d}\!u\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Since all the terms are positive and <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{u}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{u}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, it immediately follows that <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]_{s}\geq(1-e^{-s})/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]_{s}\geq(1-e^{-s})/4</annotation></semantics></math>.
Upper bounding is more delicate. Since <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}\in[0,4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}\in[0,4]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[M]_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[M]_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{1}{4}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u}(1+4G_{t(u)})(1+V_{u}^{2})\operatorname{d}\!u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(a)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{1}{4}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u}(1+4G_{t(u)})(1+V_{u}^{2})\operatorname{d}\!u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{1}{4}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u}(1+4G_{t(u)})(2+4\eta e^{(1-\epsilon)u})\operatorname{d}\!u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(b)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{1}{4}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u}(1+4G_{t(u)})(2+4\eta e^{(1-\epsilon)u})\operatorname{d}\!u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{1}{4}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u}\left(1+\frac{800}{m}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\eta}},e^{u/2}\right)\right)\left(2+4\eta e^{(1-\epsilon)u}\right)\operatorname{d}\!u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(c)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>800</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{1}{4}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u}\left(1+\frac{800}{m}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\eta}},e^{u/2}\right)\right)\left(2+4\eta e^{(1-\epsilon)u}\right)\operatorname{d}\!u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{1-e^{-(1-\epsilon)s}}{2(1-\epsilon)}+1/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(d)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\leq}}\frac{1-e^{-(1-\epsilon)s}}{2(1-\epsilon)}+1/8</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(e)}}}}}{{\leq}}3/4\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(e)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(e)}}}}}{{\leq}}3/4\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(a)</span> follows from <a href="#A5.E16" title="In Bounding the quadratic variation ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>,
<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(b)</span> from <a href="#A5.E15" title="In Bounding the quadratic variation ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>,
<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(c)</span> from <a href="#A5.E12" title="In Exact solution ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> and <a href="#A5.E13" title="In Exact solution ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>,
<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(d)</span> by computing the integral and naive bounding and <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(e)</span> is immediate.
Therefore <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-e^{-s})/2\leq[M]_{s}\leq 3/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-e^{-s})/2\leq[M]_{s}\leq 3/2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounding the SDE</h3>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our exact solution is</p>
<table id="A5.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u/2}(1+G_{t(u)})\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>96</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u/2}(1+G_{t(u)})\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u/2}\left(1+\frac{8}{m}e^{u/2}\right)\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(a)</mtext></mpadded></mover><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>96</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-(1-\epsilon)u/2}\left(1+\frac{8}{m}e^{u/2}\right)\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-u/2+\epsilon s_{\max}/2}\left(1+\frac{8}{m}e^{u/2}\right)\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(b)</mtext></mpadded></mover><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>96</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{96}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-u/2+\epsilon s_{\max}/2}\left(1+\frac{8}{m}e^{u/2}\right)\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{48}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-u/2}\left(1+\frac{8}{m}e^{u/2}\right)\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(c)</mtext></mpadded></mover><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{48}\int_{0}^{s}e^{-u/2}\left(1+\frac{8}{m}e^{u/2}\right)\operatorname{d}\!u+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{48}\left(2+\frac{8s_{\max}}{m}\right)+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(d)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{48}\left(2+\frac{8s_{\max}}{m}\right)+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(e)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{16}+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(e)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(e)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{16}+\sqrt{\eta}W_{[M]_{s}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(f)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{16}+\sqrt{\eta}(e^{-s}/4-1/8)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(f)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(f)}}}}}{{\leq}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\eta}}{16}+\sqrt{\eta}(e^{-s}/4-1/8)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(g)}}}}}{{&lt;}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\sqrt{\eta}(e^{-s}/4-1/16)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>&lt;</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(g)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(g)}}}}}{{&lt;}}e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\sqrt{\eta}(e^{-s}/4-1/16)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(a)</span> follows from <a href="#A5.E13" title="In Exact solution ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.
<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(b)</span> since <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(c)</span> since <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\epsilon s_{\max}/2)\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\epsilon s_{\max}/2)\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(d)</span> by crudely bounding the integral.
<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(e)</span> since <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 8s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 8s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(f)</span> since <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{u}\leq 1/8-u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{u}\leq 1/8-u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]_{s}\geq(1-e^{-s})/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]_{s}\geq(1-e^{-s})/4</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(g)</span> since <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\eta}\geq C\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\eta}\geq C\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, with constant probability, whenever <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t(s)}\in((1-\Delta_{2})s-1,s+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t(s)}\in((1-\Delta_{2})s-1,s+1)</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A5.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{t}=2\operatorname{arcsinh}(U_{t})\leq 2\operatorname{arcsinh}(V_{s(t)})&lt;2\operatorname{arcsinh}\left(e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\sqrt{\eta}(e^{-s}/4-1/16)\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arcsinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arcsinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arcsinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{t}=2\operatorname{arcsinh}(U_{t})\leq 2\operatorname{arcsinh}(V_{s(t)})&lt;2\operatorname{arcsinh}\left(e^{(1-\epsilon)s/2}\sqrt{\eta}(e^{-s}/4-1/16)\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which completes the proof.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We collect here the experiments in the lower bound construction in <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 10. ‣ Lower bound construction ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> but using discrete time policy gradient as outlined in <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Bandit notation ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10219v1/fig.png" id="A6.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:510/339;" width="510" height="339" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>
The plot shows 40 trajectories of <math id="A6.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t,1}</annotation></semantics></math> produced by <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Bandit notation ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> on the instance of <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 10. ‣ Lower bound construction ‣ 4 Lower bound ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> for 6 different learning rates with <math id="A6.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}=0.002" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.002</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}=0.002</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10219v1/fig-k-3.png" id="A6.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:510/339;" width="510" height="339" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>
The figure shows the results for the same experiment as in <a href="#A6.F1" title="In Appendix F Experiments ‣ A Diffusion Analysis of Policy Gradient for Stochastic Bandits" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> but with <math id="A6.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>, suggesting that the logarithmic number of arms used in the lower bound is needed.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
